<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diriyah</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dir'iyah, Ad-Dir'iyah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Diriyah is a town in Wadi Hanifa on the north-western edge of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a>, Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>. It was the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-saud">Al Saud</a> and capital of the first Saudi state from the 18th century, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-saud">Muhammad ibn Saud</a> allied with the preacher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-abd-al-wahhab">Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab</a> in 1744. Ottoman-Egyptian forces under Ibrahim Pasha destroyed it in 1818. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudbrick">mud-brick</a> district of at-Turaif is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diriyah.jpg" alt="Diriyah" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FShbib · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Riyadh_Region_-_Ad_Diriyah.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Al Saud emerged at <b>Diriyah</b> in central Arabia, where Muhammad bin Saud became emir on 22 February 1727.</blockquote><a href="/empire/saudi-arabia">Saudi Arabia · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After <b>Diriyah</b> fell in 1818, local leaders took charge, and from 1823 a series of emirs, from 1834 of the Al Aidh family, ruled the region from Abha.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-asir">Emirate of Asir</a></li><li><blockquote>Muhammad ibn Saud became emir of the small oasis town of <b>Diriyah</b> in Najd in 1727.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-diriyah">Emirate of Diriyah</a></li></ul></section>
